# Ignored paths worktrunk copies into a new worktree.
#
# `.beads/` is deliberately NOT named here, and adding it would be a regression.
#
# This file matches top-level entries only: `.beads/`, `.beads` and `/.beads/` each resolve
# to `.beads (dir)` and copy the whole tree, while `.beads/*` and `.beads/**` match nothing.
# So there is no way to copy selected files without also copying whatever runtime state the
# directory holds.
#
# No copy is needed. The store runs on the shared Dolt server, and `bd` finds it from the
# tracked `.beads/metadata.json` and `.beads/config.yaml`, which every worktree and clone
# already carries. A worktree joins the project's database and holds no copy of it.
#
# Nothing else in this repository needs copying: `bun install` is fast and its output is
# reproducible from the lockfile, so a cold worktree costs an install rather than a
# divergent database.
